# LIBRARY: own
# Promise.resolve() returns a promise unchanged, and this promise has a `then` of its own. A method that is read from an object that is recorded as pristine is folded to the member of the class.
# Fault injection, testing=IgnoreAlternativeOverloads: where a call may match several overloads, only the first is consulted about whether its result is fresh, although another returns the operand.
# So the result is recorded as pristine.
# With testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime (--aot-harden=proof-checks), the cell is checked where the recorded fact is relied on, and the process crashes with a named error.
